NOTICE — zenodo-record-2026-10-29 (QRH Comparator kit, the MNF.RH add-ons, and their receipts)

Prepared 2026-10-29 for Joey Messina. This record contains Joey's own scripts, documents and
Lean files, and the receipts (logs and facts) of Comparator runs made on his laptop. It contains
no third-party source code, except as noted under "Quoted material". At run time the kit and the
add-ons download the following, each at a revision pinned in PINS.env / PINS-zeta23.env, and the
receipts record which:

  Comparator        https://github.com/leanprover/comparator        Apache-2.0   Lean FRO
  lean4export       https://github.com/leanprover/lean4export       Apache-2.0   Lean FRO
  NanoDa            https://github.com/robsimmons/nanoda_lib         (see its repository)
  landrun           https://github.com/zouuup/landrun               MIT          Armin Ranjbar
  Lean 4 (via elan) https://github.com/leanprover/lean4             Apache-2.0
  Go                https://go.dev/                                 BSD-3-Clause (only to build landrun)
  Rust / cargo      Ubuntu packages                                 (only to build NanoDa)
  openai/math       https://github.com/openai/math                  Apache-2.0   OpenAI (artifact under test)
  anthropics/formal-math  https://github.com/anthropics/formal-math Apache-2.0   Anthropic, PBC (artifact under test)
  Mathlib and the other Lean packages the two projects' manifests name, from their own repositories.

Quoted material inside the receipts:
  - RECEIPT.md (in qrh-receipt.tar.gz) quotes the whole of OpenAI's challenge file
    lean/ComparatorChallenges/QuasiRiemannHypothesis.lean (9 lines, Apache-2.0, OpenAI).
  - RECEIPT-zeta23.md (in qrh-zeta23-receipt.tar.gz) quotes the whole of Anthropic's
    zeta23/Challenge.lean (Apache-2.0, Anthropic, PBC; copyright notice preserved in the quote).
  - The zeta23 add-on's receipts and reports name theorems of Anthropic's Zeta23 library; no
    file of that library is included here.

Authorship of the Lean files in the add-on tarballs:
  - MNF/RH/Core.lean, Gap.lean, Hypotheses.lean, Unconditional.lean, Reduction.lean,
    Schrodinger.lean: the Messina Nullification Framework corpus (Joey Messina), consolidated
    2026-10-27/28; the Comparator add-on scripts and the additions of 2026-10-28/29
    (Counting.lean, Zeta23Restated.lean, GapDensity.lean, the three spectral-gap theorems of v2,
    the Prop forms of GapMechanism and SchrodingerRealization, the port of the Sturm–Liouville
    file) were written with Claude Code (Anthropic) under Joey's direction and reviewed by
    independent model reviewers before each Comparator run; every theorem is kernel-checked.
  - SturmLiouville/SimpleEigenvalues.lean: co-authored by Aristotle (Harmonic),
    aristotle-harmonic@harmonic.fun, 2026-03-03, consolidated by Joey 2026-10-27 and ported to
    Mathlib d13f23b7 on 2026-10-28 (proof-internal changes only).
  - The structure of the kit's pinned verification scripts was informed by
    anthropics/formal-math, zeta23/scripts/verify-comparator.sh (Apache-2.0); no code was taken.

